---
description: Commit (and push, with confirmation) at logical implementation checkpoints
alwaysApply: true
---

# Commit Cadence

- After completing a logical unit of work (a feature, fix, or self-contained
  set of file changes), stage and commit it with a clear, descriptive message
  rather than letting unrelated changes pile up in one big commit.
- Prefer several small, focused commits over one large commit.
- Follow the user's existing git rules for pushing:
  - Never push directly to `main` without explicit confirmation.
  - If currently on `main`, stop and ask for confirmation before any push,
    even if the user already asked to push.
  - Otherwise, ask before pushing a commit unless the user has specifically
    asked to push.
